The numerical method is the production, full-simplex, two-fold estimator
in the BLISS research scripts Trans-AW-highdim-sim.R and
trans_aw_weight_penalty.R, as described in report_5.tex.
The package uses the simulation report's fixed multiplier of 0.01 by default.
Input handling, model summaries and predictions are package interfaces.
Only observed target and source data enter the fit.
The Biometrika simulation uses finite differences in centered log weights
as recorded in the numerical appendix of report_5.tex. The kinase analysis
uses the common-design source fit and analytic weight derivatives in the
nine-screen application. Figures and tables use the archived study fits.
